        "narrative": "Iron-55 (55Fe) is a radioactive isotope of iron with a nucleus containing 26 protons and 29 neutrons. It decays by electron capture to manganese-55 with a half-life of 2.7562 years. This decay is to the ground state of the daughter, so emits only X-rays and Auger electrons. It is sometimes used as an X-ray source for various scientific analysis methods, such as X-ray diffraction and X-ray fluorescence.",
